{
  "_doc": "Seeded PRs: one known change each, with the check a correct Carrick would post for it. The edits are the one source for both readers: tests/pr_on_main_test.rs (`apply_seed`, payload assertions) and the private PR-accuracy instrument, which replays each seed with a candidate build and the cloud's renderer and scores the posted check against `expect`. `expect` is a closed world: `rows` names every row the correct check carries (an `optional` row may be there or not), so any other row is false and a missing one is a miss. Kinds: `risk_introduced` (a contract risk the PR introduces, at its call site; `label` is the operation as the check names it), `checked_line` (\"Checked N contracts. Nothing to flag.\"), and the hidden delta kinds `delta_new`, `delta_removed`, `removed_still_called`. `title` is the title class (`no_contract_changes`, `no_contract_risks`, `risks_introduced`, `not_clean` for any title that is not one of the two clean ones). `open: true` marks a seed whose correct row has no kind yet: a row it posts is new, not false. `change` is the kind of change the seed makes, from a closed list (`shape_break`, `verb_change`, `removed_while_used`, `sender_renamed`, `delta_only`, `quiet`). `known_miss` is `{\"stage\", \"issues\"}`: `stage` is the first stage (`found`, `paired`, `judged`, `finding`, `shown`) at which today's check for the seed is wrong, `issues` the open issues it waits on (`carrick#N` or `carrick-cloud#N`). It is a test expectation, never a status: `pr_on_main_test` computes the scanner stages (found to finding) from the payload and fails when the declaration is behind or ahead of them. `retired: {date, reason}` takes a seed out of every run; a seed is never deleted without it. Edit ops: `replace` (each `from` must be in the file), `move` (git mv), `copy`, `write`, `delete`. A seed that moves lines in a file with an `__llm__/analyze-file/` answer moves the answer's lines in the same seed. This file is an answer key: never edit `expect` to make a run pass.",
